Mark, thanks for spotting that problem.  I'll pass it on to Roderick.

As for the thread generally, Hearse doesn't currently support any 64-bit 
versions of Nethack.  I tweaked the protocol a while back to make it 
easier to add support when the time comes, but currently it is probably 
simplest, as suggested, to use a 32-bit version instead.

64-bit support will come eventually, but it's a matter of getting enough 
of a critical mass to make it worth the while else it'll just be a 
handful of people swapping bones.  I'll add a comment on this to the 
Hearse web page so other people don't get caught out.

